ual footprint is under the 80% low-water mark after each `docker rm` (re-read the ledger vs subtract the reaped container's size).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: '`--reap` removes an exited unowned container when the footprint exceeds the share, nothing under it, reaps oldest-first to an 80% low-water mark'","§2i reads only the AGGREGATE Containers Reclaimable/Size from a single `docker system df` call; verified docker_ledger_bytes at observability.sh:519-555 parses Type|Size rows, which carry no per-container breakdown","To reap 'oldest-first to a low-water mark' the loop needs per-container SizeRw (e.g. `docker ps -a --size`) and a rule for when the residual footprint is under the share; the plan mentions neither, so the convergence condition and the cost of re-measuring per iteration are undefined"],"finding":"The reap loop's oldest-first-to-80%-low-water-mark termination is specified against the aggregate footprint (docker system df Containers Reclaimable), but the plan names no PER-CONTAINER size source for ordering/deciding convergence, nor whether it re-reads the ledger after each `docker rm`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc9a4b31784c203a3","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1 (`reaps oldest-first to an 80% low-water mark`) and Observability §2i","norm_id":"n6cf4412d8b51fb2e","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer estimates per-container bytes from an un-named source and mis-orders the reap, or re-runs the full `docker system df` walk after every rm and makes the 5-min tick expensive","Two containers exit with unknown relative sizes; 'oldest-first to 80%' cannot be evaluated without a per-container size"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","